@bio:

Darius Kučinskas, PhD, is an associate professor at Kaunas
University of Technology. He is a Lithuanian musicologist
and researcher whose scholarly work focuses on M. K.
Čiurlionis studies, music editing and publishing, and the
preservation of musical heritage. He has contributed
extensively to the fields of digital musicology and
historical music media research. Kučinskas is the author
and editor of several significant academic publications,
including <i>Music and Technologies</i> (2014), <i>Ethnic Piano Rolls
in the United States</i> (2021), and <i>Chronological Catalogue of
the Music of Mikalojus Konstantinas Čiurlionis</i> (2025), as
well as numerous articles on Lithuanian music culture, the
history of music publishing, and analytical interpretations
of Čiurlionis’s compositions. His research has been
presented at international conferences and world congresses
and published in Lithuanian and international peer-reviewed
scholarly journals.

@@END: BIO